# ChangeRadar — next sessions

Engine v0.2 is published. Do not restart Phase 0–6. Cosine score = lookalike ranking, not P(outage).

## Done (do not redo)

- MiniLM retrieve + CLI + Gradio + static HF Space
- Public seed 1,513 (RCAEval + Cloud-OpsBench + AnoMod labels only; no AnoMod.zip)
- Hub dataset `karthikreddyv/changeradar-incidents`; git `karthikvkreddy/changeradar` (`main`)
- Default git corpus = 18 handwritten demos only
- Mined GitHub issues: local `data/local/github/` (gitignored). Eval `--suite github` Hit@1 0.94 is same-document, not a prod claim
- User verified `score-diff`: memory-cut → inc-001 HIGH; docs-only ConfigMap typo → MED (false-ish)

## Next (in order)

- **A (this repo):** CI tests for `score-diff` / `diffparse`. Memory diff → inc-001 HIGH; docs-only must not look like an outage.
- **B (`changeradar-corpus`):** Helm-shaped change text as queries, issue as incident. Re-eval `--suite github`.
- **C (this repo):** Score the same queries against `data/public` (1.5k). Decide default index (demo vs public).
- **D (this repo):** BYO ingest of private incidents + real `helm diff`.
- **E (later):** embedding fine-tune — only after B is not same-document and C/D look worth improving.

## Do not

- Mix mined GitHub issue bodies into `data/incidents.jsonl` or the Hub dataset
- Fine-tune yet; download AnoMod.zip / LEMMA; call Hit@k an outage probability
